{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 131, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 131, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=132&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=130&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 286255202, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r286255202-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Holy hindu temple", "text": "Most tourists getting into Kathmandu, will make a visit to this temple considered a very holy shrine.\n\nThe temple is built centuries ago and is evident from the structure of the building. This temple has restrictions like no photography allowed of the main Shiva temple where the Shivling is. More so, you will need to keep your footwear at the designated place and walk to the main temple area barefeet. In case of rainy days, this becomes a little messy.\n\nThe holliness of the shrine has been well accepted by hindus over the years. The positive vibrations of the place is well evident and you will find it quite tranquil in here.\n\nAfter the massive earthquake this year, the temple structure has stood still even after 380+ aftershocks! That is quite a marvel. But on the flip side, which is also normal, is that tourism has been hit in this country and my last visit there hardly saw much visitors from abroad.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": fa